Z||000000||dennis_6||09-28-2001||09:00 AM||||I am buying a Fiero parts car in Lafayette, IN and I live in Hillsboro, Ohio.  What would be the cheapest way to get it towed here.  I have no vehicle capable of towing.  Is there any forum members who live in Indiana or Ohio who would do this fairly cheap or atleast rent me something that is capable of doing the job?||||reg||5
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||09-28-2001||09:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR>[B]What would be the cheapest way to get it towed here.  [B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Try contacting U-haul / Penski / or Ryder.<P>I've used U-haul a few times, a small truck / trailer or dolly isn't that bad.<P>Should be 'bout 80 bucks a for a one way rental (per day)<P>Drive your car there, rent the truck in that town, take a bud with you, to drive one car back, and to keep an eye on the trailer behind.<P>If you have some two way radio's, that would be a good way to keep in touch. (those are cheap also, a set can be about 45 bucks)<P>Good luck.||||reg||6
